  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Lithium nitrate when heated gives lithium oxide, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Li</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math>, whereas other alkali metal nitrates decompose to give the corresponding nitrite.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><msub><mi>LiNO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&#10230;</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>Li</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><msub><mi>NO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>NaNO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&#10230;</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>NaNO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math></p><p>However, the decomposition product of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>NaNO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> are temperature dependent process as shown in the below reaction.</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0039_549f544846ce.png\" style=\"width: 281px; height: 120px;\" /></p></blockquote>"
  }
}